title: "pallet-treasury: Asset Category"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `spend` now takes a `SpendAsset`, either `Specific(asset_kind)` or `Category(name)`, so a
      spend can request payment from a group of interchangeable assets such as USD stablecoins.
      A category payout draws from the category's assets in registration order, bounded by their
      available treasury balances; any uncovered amount stays claimable after `check_status`.

      Categories resolve through the new `frame_support` trait `AssetCategoryManager`, configured
      as `pallet_treasury::Config::AssetCategories`; use `NoAssetCategories` for specific-asset
      spends only. `pallet-assets` holds the membership storage, the `ForceOrigin` calls
      `add_to_category` and `remove_from_category`, and a `categories` genesis field.

      `PaymentState` records one execution per asset paid from, a breaking change to `Spends`.
      Runtimes with a treasury must run `pallet_treasury::migration::v1`, which translates existing
      spends and sets storage version 1. `payout` and `check_status` declare weight for the largest
      category and refund the unused portion; `payout` returns `DispatchResultWithPostInfo`.

